# Link-only force-reference: keeps the advertising-ID support alive on iOS.
#
# GoogleAppMeasurementIdentitySupport is a static archive whose AdId class
# (APMPlatformIdentitySupport) is detected by GoogleAppMeasurement at RUNTIME
# (NSClassFromString) — there is no link-time reference to it. Without forcing
# the symbol, Kotlin/Native's linker dead-strips the archive member and IDFA
# collection is silently NOT enabled in the consumer binary, defeating this
# module's sole purpose. `-u` on the class symbol forces the member to be
# linked. Propagated to the consumer's final binary via this cinterop klib.
#
# NOTE: the symbol name is a GoogleAppMeasurement internal; recheck on a
# firebase-apple version bump. If it ever disappears the consumer link fails
# loudly (undefined symbol) rather than silently regressing.
package = dev.ynagai.firebase.analytics.advertising.forcelink
linkerOpts = -u _OBJC_CLASS_$_APMPlatformIdentitySupport
